# Agent workflow

Defaults for every change, in every repository.

- Follow existing patterns in the file and service you touch; match naming, layout and error style.
- Respect the architectural layering (see the architecture rule and the scoped backend and frontend rules).
- Prefer small, focused changes; avoid drive-by refactors unrelated to the request.
- When adding cross-cutting behaviour (auth, messaging, errors), extend existing abstractions instead of inventing parallel ones.
- Do not commit secrets, `.env` values or credentials, and never paste them into rules or docs.
- Branches: `<type>/<kebab-description>` (`feature/`, `fix/`, `task/`, `chore/`, `docs/`). Commits: `<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary>` (`feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `chore`, `docs`, `test`, `perf`).
- Before finishing: run the checks for what you changed (`uv run ruff check .`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, `bash scripts/check_docs.sh`). The backend has no automated test suite; verify endpoints by hand for each role.
- Keep docs in sync: update the affected pages in `docs/` in the same change (or run `/doc-sync`), regenerate the API reference after API changes (`bash scripts/export_openapi.sh`), and add a user-facing entry to `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]`.
- When conventions change, update `docs/standards/` and the matching rule in `.agents/rules/`, then run `bash scripts/sync_agent_rules.sh`. Never edit `.claude/rules/`, `.cursor/rules/` or the generated table in `CLAUDE.md`.

Details: `docs/standards/general.md`, `docs/standards/git.md`, `docs/standards/documentation.md`, `docs/guides/testing-and-linting.md`.
